Date: 2026-10-07

This fork of the CSE 507 course repository (https://github.com/jliangclass-intro/2026Fall-CSE507-Ark-Container)
modifies Ark+ code from JLiangLab/Ark (https://github.com/JLiangLab/Ark), which reaches this fork through the course
repository (the course's Ark+ container code) and is licensed under the ASU license reproduced in LICENSE-ASU-Ark.txt;
the course repository itself has no license file. This file describes the changes, as section 5(c) of that license
requires. The changes are relative to the course repository's main branch at commit
2949b2e764b11e21c31d668efcc10cf2a33acd20. The modified Python and shell sources listed below begin with a header
comment pointing here.

Modified files inherited from the course repository

- base/engine.py: adds layer-wise LR decay parameter groups for the DINOv3 ViT, --eval_every, --clip-grad wiring and a grouped-optimizer resume check.
- base/joint_training.py: the joint-training loop measures or clips the gradient norm before each optimizer step and logs it (GN).
- base/main_ark.py: adds the vit_base_dinov3 model choice and the --eval_every, --layer-decay and --patch-embed-lr-mult options.
- base/models.py: adds ArkViT (DINOv3 ViT-B/16 with projector and heads), vit_param_groups, and a strict check of the loaded DINOv3 checkpoint keys.
- base/trainer.py: the cyclic training loop measures or clips the gradient norm before each optimizer step and logs it (GN).
- base/utils.py: adds clip_or_measure_grad_norm.
- experiment_scripts/common.sh: the shared launcher reads batch size, lr, test augmentation, evaluation cadence, workers, model, init and pretrained weights from ARK_* environment variables; the defaults reproduce the original behavior.
- README.md: prepends "About this fork", replaces the container download command with a pointer to the course repository's README, and appends "Gaudi on Sol".
- .gitignore: also ignores weights/, *.pth, *.pt, *.safetensors, .DS_Store and *.log.

Added files

New tools in base/
- base/check_dinov3_load.py: CPU smoke test for the vit_base_dinov3 backbone.
- base/convert_hf_dinov3_to_meta.py: converts a Hugging Face DINOv3 ViT-B/16 checkpoint to Meta's state-dict layout.
- base/test_dinov3_finetune_recipe.py: CPU checks for the DINOv3 fine-tuning recipe (AdamW, layer-wise LR decay, grad-norm clipping).

Vendored Meta code, under its own license
- base/dinov3/: the DINOv3 ViT from https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov3, licensed under the DINOv3 License (base/dinov3/LICENSE.md); base/dinov3/VENDORED.md records the source commit and which files were edited.

Gaudi2 (HPU) path
- containers/gaudi/: apptainer.def, requirements.txt and requirements_nodeps.txt for the Gaudi2 container.
- gaudi.sh: runs a command inside the Gaudi container (the counterpart of nvidia.sh).
- gaudi_hlsmi.sh, gaudi_check_cards.sh, gaudi_verify_busy.sh: the shared hl-smi reader, the fail-closed pre-launch card check, and the report-only busy check.
- gaudi_smoke.sh: 1-card smoke test.
- build_gaudi_image.sh: builds containers/gaudi/gaudi.sif.

Experiment scripts and launchers
- experiment_scripts/all4_concurrent_random_sampling/, all4_concurrent_random_sampling_dinov3/, all4_cyclic_dinov3_adamw/ and all4_cyclic_dinov3_v2/: start and resume scripts for the Demo 1 runs on all four datasets (VinDr-CXR, ChestX-ray14, MIMIC, CheXpert).
- run_p1_*.sh and resume_p1_*.sh in the repository root: Slurm launchers for the Practice 1 runs.
- run_d1_*.sh, resume_d1_*.sh and eval_d1_6.sh in the repository root: Slurm launchers for the Demo 1 runs and the d1_6 evaluation, including the Gaudi launchers run_d1_8a_gaudi.sh and resume_d1_8a_gaudi.sh.

